  "hypothesis": "CoreRank Method 2 discovered a low-BGE (0.706), high-ACE-mechanism (0.879, 4B transfer +12.31) bridge between ProbMoE's differentiable marginal-probability subset routing and BatchTopK Sparse Autoencoders. We test whether replacing straight-through TopK gradients with ProbMoE's calibrated marginal-selection surrogate p_j = sigmoid((z_j - tau)/T) under identical hard BatchTopK forward sparsity and pure MSE loss improves reconstruction fidelity (FVU), eliminates dead latents, and alters cross-seed feature stability on real Qwen3-1.7B residual-stream activations.",
